================================================================================
POWER BI DAX MEASURES & PARAMETER DOCUMENTATION
Project: US Commercial Payer Market Access & Patient Burden Analysis
================================================================================

1. PARAMETER TABLE: Copay Card Subsidy Schedule ($0–$500)
Purpose: What-If parameter series generating $25 monthly discount increments for commercial affordability modeling.
DAX:
Copay Card Discount = GENERATESERIES(0, 500, 25)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. MEASURE: Selected Monthly Copay Subsidy ($)
Purpose: Captures the active slider value selected by the user to drive real-time net cost and affordability simulations.
DAX:
Copay Card Discount Value = SELECTEDVALUE('Copay Card Discount'[Copay Card Discount])

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3. MEASURE: Gross Patient Out-of-Pocket Cost
Visual Card Label: Gross Monthly OOP
Purpose: Baseline monthly patient cost-sharing burden prior to any manufacturer copay card subsidy.
DAX:
Avg Patient OOP = AVERAGE(iqvia_market_access[est_patient_cost])

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. MEASURE: Net Patient OOP (Post-Copay Support)
Visual Card Label: Net Patient OOP
Purpose: Effective monthly out-of-pocket cost paid by the patient after applying the simulated manufacturer copay card discount.
DAX:
Net Patient Cost = 
AVERAGEX(
    iqvia_market_access,
    MAX(0, iqvia_market_access[est_patient_cost] - 'Copay Card Discount'[Copay Card Discount Value])
)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5. MEASURE: Coinsurance Exposure Rate (% High Barrier)
Visual Card Label: High-Barrier Plans (Coinsurance)
Purpose: Share of plans utilizing percentage-based coinsurance rather than predictable flat copays, creating high financial friction.
DAX:
% High Barrier Plans = 
DIVIDE(
    CALCULATE(COUNTROWS(iqvia_market_access), iqvia_market_access[access_tier] = "High Barrier (Coinsurance)"),
    COUNTROWS(iqvia_market_access),
    0
)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

6. MEASURE: Affordable Coverage Rate (<= $50 OOP)
Visual Card Label: Affordable Plans (<=$50)
Purpose: Share of commercial plans where net patient out-of-pocket exposure falls at or below the $50 abandonment threshold after copay assistance.
DAX:
% Affordable Plans = 
VAR Discount = 'Copay Card Discount'[Copay Card Discount Value]
RETURN
DIVIDE(
    CALCULATE(
        COUNTROWS(iqvia_market_access),
        FILTER(iqvia_market_access, (iqvia_market_access[est_patient_cost] - Discount) <= 50)
    ),
    COUNTROWS(iqvia_market_access),
    0
)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

7. MEASURE: Copay Assistance Affordability Sensitivity
Visual Chart Title: Copay Card Sensitivity: % Affordable Plans by Discount Level
Purpose: Dynamic elasticity curve modeling how affordable plan coverage scales across $0–$500/month copay card subsidy levels.
DAX:
Simulated Affordability Curve = 
VAR DiscountLevel = SELECTEDVALUE('Copay Card Discount'[Copay Card Discount])
RETURN
DIVIDE(
    CALCULATE(
        COUNTROWS(iqvia_market_access),
        FILTER(iqvia_market_access, (iqvia_market_access[est_patient_cost] - DiscountLevel) <= 50)
    ),
    COUNTROWS(iqvia_market_access),
    0
)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

8. MEASURE: Dynamic Report Header
Purpose: Context-aware banner title that updates automatically based on the active therapeutic tier selection.
DAX:
Dynamic Title = 
"Market Access & Patient Burden: " & SELECTEDVALUE('iqvia_market_access'[Drug Tier], "All Therapeutic Tiers")

================================================================================